<title>GERMANY: Hamburg air cargo rises 1.4 pct in April 97.</title>
<headline>Hamburg air cargo rises 1.4 pct in April 97.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total flown air cargo handled at Hamburg airport (HAM) in April rose 1.4 percent to 3,048 tonnes, figures from the German airports association ADV showed.</p>
<p>But air cargo at Hamburg was down 2.6 percent over the first four months of the year, the monthly ADV traffic report showed.</p>
<p>Details in tonnes with percent changes on 1996 include:</p>
<p>				April '97    Pct change</p>
<p>  Total flown cargo	3,048	  Up   1.4</p>
<p>  Exports		    1,238	  Up   2.1</p>
<p>  Imports		    1,808	  Up   1.3</p>
<p>  Transit			  2		 n/a</p>
<p>			     Jan-Apr 97    Pct change</p>
<p>  Total flown cargo     11,771	  Down 2.6</p>
<p>  Exports		    4,623	  Down 4.5</p>
<p>  Imports		    7,135	  Down 0.8</p>
<p>  Transit			 13		 n/a</p>
<p>Source: German Airports Association ADV, market research dept.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax +5017</p>
</text>
